# Azure Blob Storage SAS Token (without leading '?')
# To generate a SAS token:
# 1. Go to Azure Portal → Your Storage Account
# 2. Navigate to "Shared access signature" under Security + networking
# 3. Configure permissions (Read, List recommended for public images)
# 4. Set expiry date
# 5. Click "Generate SAS and connection string"
# 6. Copy the SAS token (everything after the '?')
#
# Example format (DO NOT use this, generate your own):
NEXT_PUBLIC_BLOB_SAS_TOKEN=sv=2024-11-04&ss=bfqt&srt=sco&sp=rwdlacupiytfx&se=2026-11-18T20:34:53Z&st=2025-09-12T12:19:53Z&spr=https,http&sig=KNQs7rhe81AeQfnd%2BS4QMPWWo55VbNICTufFVYe5KhA%3D

